#pragma once
#include <vector>

/* Replace every element of x with the square of its value.
   Example:

   input: [5, 1, 2, -4, 8]
   output: [25, 1, 4, 16, 64]
*/
void squareEach(std::vector<int> &x) {
    for (auto &i : x) {
        i *= i;
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
The code snippet is a simple function that takes a vector of integers and replaces every element with the square of its value. The function uses a for loop to iterate through the vector and multiply each element by its square. The function is optimized by using the ```auto``` keyword to automatically deduce the type of the loop variable. The ```auto``` keyword is a C++11 feature that allows the programmer to write more concise code.

